      "writtenOn": "2022-09-02T07:40:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, that would be good way to got about it. \n\nIn terms of bazel build issue, we see emscripten has built-in support for SDL1, and tries to use that while building in our toolchain.\nhttps://emscripten.org/docs/compiling/Building-Projects.html?#using-libraries\nForcing use of SDL2, with coopts and linkopts flags is not proving workable.\n\nI was wondering what would be the best thing to do here,\n1. Make our current sk_app have a sdl1 port instead of sdl2 ? Maybe we need to use the older surface/windows API\u0027s then.\n2. Wait for emscripten to have built-in support for sdl2 ?\n3. Something else ?",
      "parentUuid": "3295e0ad_668f0b1b",
      "revId": "4940a87e5bc7ff2b2749f791ee39af365d2f9f29",
